{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.QuantumCharacteristicClassesUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.QuantumCharacteristicClassesUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.QuantumCharacteristicClassDisplay"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumCharClasses.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumCharClasses.unique","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-characteristic-classes-unique.lean#L38-L61","doc":"**Uniqueness of quantum characteristic classes (proved\nextensionality).**\n\nTwo `QuantumCharacteristicClass` terms at the same brane-tower\nlevel with the same obstruction space, additive-group structure,\nand obstruction value are equal.  Replaces a false\n`Subsingleton QuantumCharacteristicClass` axiom (`level` alone\nseparates instances); the cohomology-quotient classification is\nthe open refactor. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:quantum-characteristic-classes-unique","label":"prop:quantum-characteristic-classes-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-characteristic-classes-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}